; ============================================================================
; CSpect debug script — G46(b) NextZXOS supervisor entry state dump
;
; HOW TO USE:
;   1. Boot NextZXOS in CSpect normally (TBBlue splash → press SPACEBAR or wait)
;   2. Open the CSpect debugger (F1 by default)
;   3. Either:
;      a) Paste the commands below one block at a time, OR
;      b) Load this file via the debugger's script-load command if available
;   4. Save the debugger output (right-click → "Save log" or copy/paste to file)
;   5. Send the output back so I can seed --bypass-tbblue-fw post-handoff init
;
; CSpect debugger commands used here (v2.x reference):
;   bp <addr>     — set breakpoint
;   bp on <addr>  — alternate syntax
;   g             — go (continue execution)
;   r             — show all Z80 registers + flags
;   m <addr> <n>  — memory dump, n bytes from <addr>
;   nr            — dump current NextReg state (or `nr <reg>` for one)
;   ?             — help
;
; If your version uses different commands, the equivalents are usually:
;   "bp 00EF"  →  breakpoint at PC=0x00EF
;   "m 5B00 256"  →  dump 256 bytes from $5B00
;   register dump and NR dump are usually visible in dedicated windows you
;   can screenshot.
; ============================================================================


; ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
; STEP 1 — set breakpoint at supervisor entry $00EF
; ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
bp 00EF


; ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
; STEP 2 — restart the machine and let it run until BP fires
; (do this manually in CSpect: hard reset / restart, then "g" to continue)
; ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
g


; ============================================================================
; STEP 3 — when BP fires at PC=$00EF (FIRST HIT), run the commands below.
; Save the entire debugger output buffer / scrollback before continuing.
; ============================================================================


; --- 3a. Z80 register file ---
; Shows AF, BC, DE, HL, IX, IY, SP, AF', BC', DE', HL', PC, I, R, IM, IFF1/2
r


; --- 3b. Full NextReg dump ---
; CSpect has a NextReg window — screenshot it OR list each register:
nr 00
nr 01
nr 02
nr 03
nr 04
nr 05
nr 06
nr 07
nr 08
nr 09
nr 0A
nr 0B
nr 10
nr 12
nr 13
nr 14
nr 15
nr 16
nr 17
nr 18
nr 19
nr 1A
nr 1B
nr 1C
nr 1E
nr 1F
nr 22
nr 23
nr 26
nr 27
nr 30
nr 31
nr 32
nr 33
nr 35
nr 36
nr 37
nr 38
nr 39
nr 40
nr 41
nr 42
nr 43
nr 44
nr 4A
nr 4B
nr 4C
nr 50
nr 51
nr 52
nr 53
nr 54
nr 55
nr 56
nr 57
nr 5A
nr 5B
nr 5C
nr 60
nr 61
nr 62
nr 63
nr 64
nr 68
nr 69
nr 6A
nr 6B
nr 6C
nr 6E
nr 6F
nr 70
nr 71
nr 75
nr 76
nr 77
nr 78
nr 79
nr 7F
nr 80
nr 81
nr 82
nr 83
nr 84
nr 85
nr 86
nr 87
nr 88
nr 89
nr 8A
nr 8C
nr 8E
nr 8F
nr 90
nr 91
nr 92
nr 93
nr 98
nr 99
nr 9A
nr 9B
nr A0
nr A2
nr A8
nr A9
nr B8
nr B9
nr BA
nr BB
nr C0
nr C2
nr C3
nr C4
nr C5
nr C6
nr C8
nr C9
nr CA
nr CC
nr CD
nr CE
nr D8
nr D9
nr DA


; --- 3c. NextZXOS sysvar block at $5B00..$5BFF (256 bytes) ---
; Critical: $5B69 (last RAM-test bank), $5B8A/$5B8E (wrapper save area)
m 5B00 256


; --- 3d. Canonical ZX-system sysvar block at $5C00..$5CFF (256 bytes) ---
; Critical: $5C36 (CURCHL), $5C38, $5C3A (= IY base), $5C4F, $5C51 (CHANS),
; $5C7B (STKBOT), $5C7F (machine cfg), $5CB2 (E_LINE), $5CB4
m 5C00 256


; --- 3e. Stack snapshot — 64 bytes around SP ---
; Hard-coded for typical post-init SP=$5BFF; if your SP differs, adjust.
; If your CSpect supports register-relative dumps:
;     m sp-16 64
; otherwise use the literal address from `r` output above.
m 5BE0 64


; --- 3f. Slot 7 high half ($E000..$FFFF, 8 KB) ---
; This depends on which bank NR_57 maps at this moment. Captures whatever's
; visible to the supervisor right now.
m E000 2048
m E800 2048
m F000 2048
m F800 2048


; --- 3g. (OPTIONAL) Slot 5 area $A000..$A150 ---
; The supervisor's sprite buffer build site. Captures what's there at
; supervisor entry (likely zero / random pre-init state).
m A000 336


; --- 3h. (OPTIONAL) Page 0x30 contents at $E000-$E100 if NR_57=$10 ---
; This is the page our jnext reads as zeros and that drives the bank-2
; sprite-iterator at $0EAD to compute IX. If CSpect has non-zero data
; here, this is the smoking gun.
; Already captured by 3f above unless NR_57 changes.


; ============================================================================
; STEP 4 — (OPTIONAL) capture the SECOND $00EF hit
; ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
; Our jnext trace shows 657 $00EF hits — supervisor re-enters $00EF
; periodically. The SECOND hit's state (compared to the FIRST) tells us
; what changed during the first iteration. If you have time:
;   1. After saving the FIRST-hit dump, type:  g
;   2. When the BP fires AGAIN, repeat ALL of step 3 (r + nr + m blocks).
;   3. Save the second dump separately.
;
; ============================================================================


; ============================================================================
; STEP 5 — disable BP and resume normal boot (welcome screen should render)
; ============================================================================
bp off 00EF
g


; ============================================================================
; FORMAT NOTES
; ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
; If your CSpect doesn't accept this exact syntax, the commands you need are
; semantically:
;   - "set breakpoint at 0x00EF, fire on first hit"
;   - "show all Z80 registers including alt set + IX + IY + SP + I + R + IM"
;   - "dump 256 bytes from 0x5B00"
;   - "dump 256 bytes from 0x5C00"
;   - "dump 64 bytes from SP-16"  (or from address shown in `r`)
;   - "dump 8192 bytes from 0xE000"
;   - "dump all 256 NextReg values" (NR 0x00..0xFF)
;
; If a wholesale "dump all NR" command is available (e.g. nrdump, nx, allnr),
; replace the long `nr 00 ... nr DA` list with that single command.
;
; If memory-dump is interactive and shows hex+ASCII like CSpect's default,
; that's perfect — just copy the scrollback and send.
; ============================================================================
